# Tu Captes — core agent rule

You are building **Tu Captes**: a calm cultural journey through web codes, powered by quiz mechanics — **not** a quiz-app product.

## Always

- Optimize for **named concept capture** and emotional return to the **fil**
- Keep bottom nav **« Jouer »**
- Prefer Content Density / editorial substance over new UI surfaces
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/product/PRODUCT_VISION.md` when unsure

## Never (without explicit user OK)

- Schema migrations / new tables
- Mascot, map, 3D world, visible territory taxonomies
- Mass auto-tagging of `concept_key`
- Heavy gamification (guilt streaks, scoreboard-first UX)
- Reworking Fil Continu (already shipped)

## Execution bias

- Creator is often non-technical now: **implement**, then summarize briefly
- One wave at a time; stop and ask only on schema or irreversible prod risk
- Visual QA: use screenshots / Playwright — do not claim the UI “looks good” without evidence
